Slackware From Seed (SFS) kit
=============================

Builds Slackware64 (development branch) from its own source tree, inside a
chroot, without network once the preparation is done.  Default scope: the
a, ap, d, l, n, tcl series and the kernel, plus the x, xap and kde packages
those need.  No desktop environments.

Follow GUIDE.md.  Everything is done with one command:

  ./sfs doctor      check the host, sfs.conf, the tree and the kit
  ./sfs prepare     build data, plan, risk check, seeds   (network)
  ./sfs stage0      temporary toolchain                   (root)
  ./sfs build       stage1, pass1, pass2, then verify     (root)
  ./sfs status | log [-f] | report | verify | enter | umount | plan | provides | kernels

REFERENCE.md explains what ./sfs does underneath: every step, every script,
how the build order is computed and how to fix a build that fails.

The build order is not written by hand.  sfs-plan.sh (gen.py) computes it
from the data in data/ (what every official package links against, which
package has which command and .pc file, what python packages need to build)
plus what was learned by building (manual.tsv, base.list, overrides/).
NOTES is the log of every problem met on the way and how it was solved;
DISCOVERED-DEPS.tsv lists every dependency that had to be found by building.

Files
-----
  sfs                    the one command (see above)
  GUIDE.md               what to follow
  REFERENCE.md           how it works, piece by piece
  sfs-logo.svg, .png     the logo
  sfs.conf.example       settings (copy to sfs.conf)
  sfs-kernels.sh         the kernel series of the tree (./sfs kernels)
  sfs-binindex.sh        data/binindex.tsv from the packages of slackware64/
  sfs-pcindex.sh         data/pcindex.tsv from the packages of slackware64/
  sfs-pybuild.py         data/pybuild.tsv from the tree's python tarballs
  sfs-plan.sh, gen.py    compute the build lists into plan/
  sfs-risks.py, risks.ok where the build would stop (switches in cycles,
                         downloads), with the fix; run by sfs-plan.sh
  sfs-seeds.sh           fetch everything the offline build needs
  sfs-stage0.sh          stage 0 on the host (LFS ch. 5 and 6)
  sfs-chroot.sh          mount, enter (offline) and umount the chroot
  sfs-stage0-chroot.sh   stage 0 in the chroot (LFS ch. 7)
  sfs-build.sh           run a build list; pass1/pass2 go on after a failure,
                         retry, and write a report
  sfs-orphans.sh         files no package owns (--move, --shadow)
  sfs-provides.py        which package provides a missing file, command, .pc
                         or library, and where it is in the build lists
  sfs-verify.py          optional: compare packages with the official ones
  sfs-deps-export.py     run-time + build-time dependencies of every built
                         package: TSV, an offline HTML page, an SQLite table
  base.list              stage 1 order
  manual.tsv             dependencies nobody can see, !skip, !again
  overrides/all/         SlackBuild fixes for every pass (offline, no TeX ...)
  overrides/pass1/       SlackBuild changes for stage 1 and pass 1 (cycles)
  tools/                 helpers the overrides and the build use
  data/                  depgraph.db and the indexes (./sfs prepare remakes them)
  seeds/                 filled by ./sfs prepare (see seeds/README)
  NOTES                  the build log of this kit
  DISCOVERED-DEPS.tsv    dependencies found by building
